WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.834
Validity and accuracy are related but different
Validity asks whether

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:11.617
a value fits a documented rule Accuracy asks whether
the value

00:00:11.643 --> 00:00:17.429
reflects reality A temperature can fall inside an
allowed range and still

00:00:17.442 --> 00:00:23.214
be inaccurate because of a sensor problem or
data-entry error Validity

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:28.966
is often easier to automate Accuracy may require
comparison with the source system

00:00:29.177 --> 00:00:35.050
another measurement or domain knowledge This
distinction prevents us from assuming

00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:38.050
that passing a validation rule proves the value is
true
